course: dictionary
lesson: 11392
title: A formal word: accede
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Accede is a formal word. You will not hear it in playground chat, but you will meet it in history books, news reports and exam texts. Its plain meanings are agree, give in, and become king or queen.
explain: «The head teacher did not want a trip to the zoo, but in the end she acceded to the class's request.» The clue is request: she said no at first, then said yes. So acceded means agreed, or gave in to what the class asked for.
explain: Accede is almost always followed by to, as in accede to a request or accede to the throne. Read the words around it: is someone giving way to pressure, or taking up an important job? Then swap in a plain word and check the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Accede means to agree to a request or demand, often after first not wanting to.
fact: Accede can also mean to take up an important position, especially becoming king or queen: «She acceded to the throne.»
fact: Accede can mean a country joins an agreement or organisation: «The country acceded to the treaty.»
fact: Plain swaps for accede are agree, give in, become king or queen, and join.
fact: Accede is a formal word, so it is more common in writing than in talking.
exercise: «The council did not agree at first, but in the end it acceded to the villagers' demand for a new bus stop.» What does acceded mean here? | *Agreed to | Painted | Forgot | Ran away from
exercise: «When the old king died, his eldest son acceded to the throne.» What does acceded to the throne mean? | Left the castle | Sat down for a rest | *Became king | Built a new throne
exercise: Which plain word could replace acceded in «The country acceded to the agreement»? | Hid | Argued | Forgot | *Joined
test: «After weeks of pressure, the club acceded to the fans' demands and reopened the stand.» What does acceded mean? | Forgot | Refused | Argued | *Gave in
test: «The country acceded to the agreement» means the country did what? | Left the agreement | *Joined the agreement | Wrote the agreement | Ignored the agreement
exam: Tom's mum said no to a puppy, but after much asking she acceded to his request. Which word best shows what acceded means? | Shouted | *Agreed | Argued | Complained
